-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Decision functions answer `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words (a flat negative, a "means" definition, a "where", "in the case of",
--                "unless" or "at" not met).
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer (a scope limit, a list that is not closed, a bare "must" not done).
-- O 3 r 2(1) is a caveat on every answer (the Court may order otherwise in the interests of justice).
-- The Limited Liability Partnerships Act is not among the sources: its facts are inputs.

